      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Waluipedia cast sheet — Fawthful.</em> Built by <code>tools/build-character-sheets.py</code>, hand-authored from the article. no XP ledger entry; archetype default → a level 4 Artificer player-character sheet (a player may take this seat; the authored CR 4 stands in where the ledger is silent). Numbers are a GM-ready reading of the record, not a filed stat line; the article stays the authority. Archive date 1040 BF.</p><p><strong>The Usurper at Bowser's Gate</strong> — Fawthful's Forces</p><p>Status: Historical actor — identified in the 18 Harvestide, 1035 BF Bowser Castle filings; current whereabouts not established</p><p>The historical record identifies Fawthful as the commander who turned a compromised Bowser's Castle into an invasion route. With Mimbus, Cackletta, a dragon, Magikoopas, and defecting Koopa troops in the field, Fawthful treated the throne as a temporary obstacle on the way to ruling the world—or being worshipped by it.</p><h3>Evidence</h3><ul><li><strong>Headgear Ray</strong> — “Unknown — hostile commander”</li><li><strong>Extra Attack</strong> — “Unknown — hostile commander”</li><li><strong>Compromised Access</strong> — “The historical record identifies Fawthful as the commander who turned a compromised Bowser's Castle into an invasion route.”</li><li><strong>Moving Terror Weapon</strong> — “The operation began with compromised access, used a dragon as a moving terror weapon, and turned the castle's own garrison into a question Bowser could not answer quickly enough.”</li><li><strong>Not Resolved as Fawful</strong> — “The archive keeps Fawthful distinct from the older Fawful record because the assault account uses this name and does not resolve whether it is a new identity, a title, or a deliberate distortion.”</li></ul><p>Article: <code>#/article/fawthful</code> (characters). Site sheet: <code>#/sheets/fawthful</code>.</p>",
        "public": ""
      }
